@startuml InviteOriginStatusModel

title Invite origin (how they arrived) vs status (latest answer)

state "origin" as Origin {
  [*] --> ADMIN_INVITED : admin invite
  [*] --> VOLUNTEER_JOINED : open join
  [*] --> VOLUNTEER_APPLIED : later slice (enum only)
}

state "status (nullable = waiting)" as Status {
  [*] --> waiting : insert / re-invite
  waiting --> VOLUNTEER_ACCEPTED : volunteer says yes
  waiting --> VOLUNTEER_REJECTED : volunteer declines offer
  waiting --> ADMIN_REJECTED : admin withdraws outstanding
  waiting --> ADMIN_ACCEPTED : later slice (enum only)
  VOLUNTEER_ACCEPTED --> VOLUNTEER_CANCELLED : volunteer leaves seat
  VOLUNTEER_JOINED_seat --> VOLUNTEER_CANCELLED : volunteer leaves seat
  VOLUNTEER_ACCEPTED --> ADMIN_CANCELLED : admin kicks seat
  VOLUNTEER_JOINED_seat --> ADMIN_CANCELLED : admin kicks seat
  ADMIN_REJECTED --> waiting : admin re-invite\n(origin = ADMIN_INVITED)
  ADMIN_CANCELLED --> waiting : admin re-invite\n(origin = ADMIN_INVITED)
}

note right of Origin
  origin is set on insert.
  Unchanged after, except re-invite
  sets origin = ADMIN_INVITED.
  Nullable only for legacy
  ADMIN_REJECTED / CANCELLED rows.
end note

note right of Status
  Participating this slice:
  VOLUNTEER_JOINED + null
  ADMIN_INVITED + VOLUNTEER_ACCEPTED
  (later: VOLUNTEER_APPLIED + ADMIN_ACCEPTED,
  ADMIN_INVITED + ADMIN_ACCEPTED)
  Instance cancel does not stamp person-invites.
end note

@enduml
